# Source of the ArcGIS Hosted Feature Layer containing the Lima building
# footprints. Each building needs an OCC_TYPE field (its use category, e.g.
# "residential", "office", "hospitality" — see data/LIMA_OCC_TYPE.csv and
# scripts/classify_occ_type.py) — the app computes the full 24-hour
# occupancy curve live from that one field, it doesn't read per-hour data.
#
# This can be either:
#   1. A FeatureServer layer REST URL, e.g. ".../FeatureServer/0", or
#   2. An ArcGIS portal item page URL, e.g. ".../home/item.html?id=<32-char id>"
#      (the app resolves the portal item to its underlying layer automatically).
VITE_FEATURE_LAYER_URL="https://geospatialcenter.bd.esri.com/portal/home/item.html?id=e3a43660f29d4b7dad245add7324be53#overview"
